Talbot Hotel Midleton, part of the Talbot Collection, are currently recruiting for a Kitchen Porter to join our team. The successful candidate will be a team player, be flexible and must be available to work mid-week & weekends and upto 39 hours per week.
The Talbot Collection are one of the
Best Places to Work in Hospitality 2025
as awarded by the Great Place to Work. Come experience it for yourself and join our team.
Main Duties:
To ensure that the kitchen is maintained to an acceptable standard of hygiene at all times;
Areas of responsibility: a) pot wash b) pot/pan storage areas c) Kitchen/larder areas and surrounds d) Rubbish skip areas e) Hygiene in kitchen and storage areas f) wash up area g)staffing areas
To ensure that all crockery is cleaned and available for the departments as they are required;
To assist chefs in any duties, as required;
Work positively within the team;
The successful candidate must have:
Previous experience in a similar role within a hotel environment would be a distinct advantage;
A communicative level of English;
Be a team player;
Be able to work on own initiative;
Be able to work under pressure;
Available to work midweek and weekend shifts.
Some of the benefits of joining the team:
One of the Best Places to Work in Hospitality 2024 as awarded by the Great Place Work
Join a company and culture that put their team first
Training and Development Opportunities - we invest in our people
Being part of a progressive & growing company.
Contributory company pension scheme. (12 months service requirement);
Company Life Insurance Scheme
Free parking
Staff meals
Employee Assistance Programme
Talbot Collection Friends and Family Rates on accommodation
Bike to Work
Christmas Savings Scheme
*** Talbot Hotel Midleton, part of the Talbot Collection is an equal opportunities employer ***

